{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2979","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2979","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2979\",\"parent_revision\":\"0f8faa6a29de26ba576e6582e9bc5cbbbb0ba3f8bbe84710abfd9a6c9c2c1f03\",\"root_revision\":\"0f8faa6a29de26ba576e6582e9bc5cbbbb0ba3f8bbe84710abfd9a6c9c2c1f03\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Bug\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-18\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nBacklog item section names are referenced as free-form prose strings across skill/agent markdown (as both backlog_groom write directives with a section= argument, and sections[...] read lookups), with no single canonical source of truth validating that a name an agent is told to write actually matches the name a downstream consumer is told to read. This has already produced two concrete, evidence-verified defect classes.\\n\\nDefect class 1 \u2014 read-side lookups use a third, non-codified string format that matches neither valid key form. backlog_view's sections dict is keyed either by the snake_case storage key (e.g. impact_radius) or, after PR #2971's fix, by the Title Case display key (e.g. Impact Radius) produced by the display-title resolver in backlog_core/rendering.py. But the following reference docs instruct agents to read a THIRD format \u2014 lowercase with literal spaces, which never matches either: plugins/development-harness/skills/rt-ica/SKILL.md lines 75-76 (keys: acceptance criteria, expected behavior, impact radius), plugins/development-harness/skills/discovery/SKILL.md lines 32-33 (keys: acceptance criteria, expected behavior, scope, desired structure), and plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/groom-check.md line 62 (key: impact radius, with a fallback to a resources key that is itself display-title-cased post-#2971 and so also fails to match the lowercase literal). Every one of these lookups silently returns nothing (Python dict .get() semantics, no KeyError) rather than surfacing an error \u2014 an agent following these instructions gets no data and no diagnostic, and the RT-ICA/discovery extraction step this feeds into silently proceeds with incomplete information. Confirmed via direct grep against the current repo; not fixed by either PR #2971 or PR #2964, both of which correctly key on Title Case display titles but do not touch these three consumer docs.\\n\\nDefect class 2 \u2014 the section-name vocabulary itself has multiple, disagreeing definitions and no automated check that they agree. plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-layers/KNOWN_ENTITIES.md is explicitly an agent-maintained \\\"Living Document\\\" (per its own Living Document Protocol section) intended to be the canonical registry of known section names, sourced from skills/backlog/references/item-schema.md and docs/backlog-item-groomed-schema.md. It lists three separate, only-partially-overlapping name sets (top-level canonical order; mandatory Groomed subsections; optional/context-dependent sections) but is stamped \\\"last generated on 2026-06-11 from source\\\" \u2014 over two months stale relative to current work. Cross-checking it against backlog_core/rendering.py's SECTION_HEADING registry (as introduced by PR #2964) finds real names on each side the other is missing: KNOWN_ENTITIES.md lists Scope, Output / Evidence, Skills, Agents, Prior Work, Decision, Desired Structure, Human Input, Questions for Human, Blockers, Acceptance Criteria Verification, and Research First with no matching SECTION_HEADING entry; conversely SECTION_HEADING registers Concerns and Execution Results (confirmed live and current via grep of implement-feature/SKILL.md, execution/SKILL.md, complete-implementation/references/final-handoff.md) and Story, Context, Working Register, and Divergence Notes, none of which appear as a section= write directive anywhere in current plugins/development-harness/**/*.md \u2014 their only evidence is indirect, from a review agent's report of large counts (unknown__story x352, unknown__context x352) in the live .dh backlog cache, i.e. legacy production data with no current doc explaining it.\\n\\nImpacted functionality: at least two real, already-written workflow gates depend on exact-match section-name reads to make blocking decisions \u2014 groom-check.md's Priority-effort gate (Criterion 2 in feasibility-gate.md gates a BLOCKED verdict on effort/priority mismatch by reading a Priority key) and groom-drift.md (reads Impact Radius and Files keys to classify file drift). A prose-level naming mismatch between what one agent writes and what another agent's doc tells it to read is currently invisible until someone manually traces the actual runtime dict keys \u2014 there is no lint, test, or generation step that fails when a skill or agent doc's section-name string does not match the canonical registry.\\n\\nExpected outcome: every section-name string an agent is instructed to write should be readable, without silent loss, by every consumer instructed to read it back, against one canonical, current vocabulary \u2014 with no lookup silently returning nothing for a name that was actually written.\\n\\n**User-provided context** (candidate directions surfaced during investigation, not a required approach): correcting the three lowercase-with-spaces reads to Title Case; reconciling KNOWN_ENTITIES.md against SECTION_HEADING and actual doc usage in both directions; adding a validation step that fails when a doc references a section name outside the canonical registry.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **section names referenced as free-form prose strings across skill/agent docs \u2014 no canonical source of truth, silent read-side mismatches** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Description\\n\\n<div><sub>2026-08-18T09:29:23.013506Z</sub>\\n